Study Planner App instructions file

Overview
The Study Planner App is an Android application designed to help students organise and manage their study sessions.
It allows users to create subjects, schedule study sessions, add notes, and track completion status.

Features
- User login and sign up
- Create and manage subjects
- Add study sessions with date and time
- Edit sessions
- delete sessions
- Mark sessions as completed
- Persistent data storage
- read some motivational quotes
-vew all upcoming and completed sessions

Technologies Used
- Java
- Android Studio
- Room Database
- SharedPreferences
- XML

User Authentication
The application uses SharedPreferences to store user login details locally on the device.
This allows each user to access and manage their own study data.

Data Storage
The app uses the Room Database library to store subjects and study sessions.
Each session includes a title, description, date, time, username, and completion status.

